<!-- A hands-on tour. Put your cursor on a task and press the key. Ctrl+Z undoes anything. -->

# tsk — interactive tour

Every `- [ ]` line is a task; `Alt`+a key changes it and tsk fills in the id and timestamps. Press `F5` to open this in the dev host, then work down the page. One `Ctrl+Z` undoes any change.

## 1. Status

| Key | Status |
|-----|--------|
| `Alt+A` | todo `[ ]` |
| `Alt+S` | in progress `[/]` |
| `Alt+C` | done `[x]` |
| `Alt+X` | cancelled `[!]` |
| `Alt+N` | note `[n]` |

Same key toggles back. `Alt+A` turns a bare line — or a checkbox-less `- bullet` — into a task; on an empty `- [ ]` it removes it.

Try `Alt+A` on the bare line and the bare bullet (it becomes `- [ ] …`, the marker is never doubled), then `Alt+S` / `Alt+C` / `Alt+N` on the tasks — `Alt+S`/`C`/`N` flip any task's marker (same key flips back):

buy milk

- water the plants

- [ ] flip me with Alt+S <!-- @id:first-flip -->
- [x] un-complete me with Alt+C <!-- @id:first-done @completed:2026-05-27T09:00:00+08:00 -->

## 2. Priority

| Key | Priority |
|-----|----------|
| `Alt+1` | high |
| `Alt+2` | medium |
| `Alt+3` | low |

Colors the whole line; the same number clears it.

- [ ] ship the release <!-- @id:pri-a -->
- [ ] water the plants <!-- @id:pri-b -->

## 3. Tags

`#tag`, nest with `/`. Type `#` to autocomplete (from your tasks + this folder's `tags.yml`); try `proj`, `inv`, `decl`:

- [ ] sketch the architecture #
- [ ] order the parts #

`Alt+T` → searchable tag list with counts → opens a search of matching tasks. Its sibling **Tsk: Find All Tasks by Status** (Command Palette) does the same by status marker — pick `[/]` to find every in-progress task, `[x]` every done one, and so on.

Tagged something that isn't in `tags.yml` yet? **Tsk: Add Discovered Tags to tags.yml** (Command Palette) appends every such tag as a bare stub under a dated header, ready for you to give it a description or parent.

- [ ] chase the ticket #JIRAID-123 <!-- @id:tag-a -->
- [ ] mount the NAS #inventory/homelab/nas1 <!-- @id:tag-b -->

`JIRAID-123` above is also a **link** — this folder's `.vscode/settings.json` has an autolink rule (regex → URL), so Ctrl/Cmd+Click opens the ticket.

## 4. Links

| Key | Link |
|-----|------|
| `Alt+P` | `@parent` |
| `Alt+D` | `@dependsOn` |
| `Alt+R` | `@relatedTo` |

Each opens a picker; the same key removes. Linked tasks grow code lenses (`parent: …`, `children: 2`) — click to jump or peek.

Parent + two children — look at the lenses:

- [ ] plan the launch <!-- @id:link-parent -->
- [ ] book the venue <!-- @id:link-child-1 @parent:link-parent -->
- [ ] send the invites <!-- @id:link-child-2 @parent:link-parent -->

Try `Alt+D` here, pick "plan the launch":

- [ ] arrange the catering <!-- @id:link-dep -->

## 5. Structure

| Key | Effect |
|-----|--------|
| `Enter` (end of line) | new sibling task below |
| `Enter` (empty task) | outdent, or remove at the margin |
| `Tab` (empty task) | indent one level |
| `Shift+Tab` | outdent |
| `Backspace` (empty task) | degrade to a bare `- ` bullet |
| `Backspace` (empty `- `) | strip the bullet, leaving the indent |
| `Shift+Alt+↓` / `Shift+Alt+↑` | duplicate the line; the copy gets a fresh `@id`, content selected to retype |
| double-click a marker / indent | select the whole block (its *text* → just a word) |
| `Ctrl+C` / `Ctrl+X` (nothing selected) | copy / cut the whole block, sub-items and all |

Bare bullets (a `- ` item with no `[ ]`) get the same `Enter` / `Tab` / `Shift+Tab` treatment minus the checkbox — handy for notes nested under a task. Duplicate any task above with `Shift+Alt+↓`: the copy is stamped with a new `@id` (so it doesn't shadow the original) and its content lands selected — just type to rename it.

Double-click the marker or indentation of the parent below to grab it *and* its indented child at once — double-click the *text* and you still get a single word, exactly like double-clicking a `{` vs. a word in code. With nothing selected, `Ctrl+C` / `Ctrl+X` copy / cut that whole block too (**Tsk: Select Task Block** is the keyboard version).

- [ ] first step <!-- @id:indent-a -->
- [ ] Enter here for a fresh task, then Tab to indent it <!-- @id:indent-b -->
    - [ ] Shift+Tab walks me back out <!-- @id:indent-c -->
    - a bare bullet (no checkbox) — try Enter / Backspace here

## 6. Hover

Hover a task to read its id, timestamps ("3 hours ago"), tags, and links.

- [/] migrate the database #project/tsk <!-- @id:hover-demo @created:2026-05-24T09:00:00+08:00 @started:2026-05-25T11:00:00+08:00 -->

## 7. Broken links

A reference to a missing id gets a yellow squiggle. `Ctrl+.` → remove or replace it.

- [ ] dangling parent <!-- @id:broken-demo @parent:this-id-does-not-exist -->

## 8. Move

`Alt+M` → picker (or submit empty for "moved, no target") → marks `[>]`. Pick a target and the task gains an `@movedTo` plus a `movedTo: <id>` lens (the `forward` codicon) — click it to jump to where the work went. `@movedTo` is a real graph edge: the target shows a `movedHereFrom: N` lens back, and a `@movedTo` pointing at an unknown id squiggles like any broken reference.

- [ ] belongs in another project <!-- @id:move-demo -->

**Tsk: Move Task to File…** is different — it *relocates* a task (and its indented sub-items) to another `.tsk` file. Run it from the Command Palette, or `Ctrl+.` → *Move task to file…*, on the task below and pick a file (or make a new one): the task keeps its `@id` so every link still resolves, its child rides along, and a `[>]` breadcrumb stays here pointing (`@movedTo`) at its new home. Don't want the breadcrumb? **Tsk: Extract Task to File…** does the same relocation but deletes the original outright — nothing stays behind.

- [ ] relocate me to another file <!-- @id:movefile-demo -->
    - [ ] my child rides along <!-- @id:movefile-child @parent:movefile-demo -->

Coming **from Markdown**? **Tsk: Send All Markdown Tasks to Tsk File…** evacuates an `.md` checklist into tsk — markers remapped, timestamps recovered from git history. Try it on `migrate-sample.md` in this folder; details in the README's *Migrating from Markdown*.

## 9. Copy id

`` Alt+` `` copies the task's `@id`.

- [ ] copy my id <!-- @id:copy-demo -->

## 10. Paste image

`Ctrl+V` an image → saved to disk + a Markdown link inserted (alt text selected). Select text first to name it (subfolders allowed). `Ctrl+Z` removes the link and the file together.

<!-- paste an image on the line below -->

## 11. Now

| Key | Effect |
|-----|--------|
| `Alt+W` | mark the task as your current "now" |

`Alt+W` stamps a missing `@id`, flips the task to `[/]` (stamping `@started`, just like `Alt+S`), and pushes it onto a persistent undo-**tree** of "what am I working on now" — the marked line gets a border around it. Open the tree from the `target` button in this editor's title bar (or **Tsk: Open Now Stack**); it docks beside the file like a Markdown preview — click a node to jump straight back to it.

Mark the first line, then the second (it becomes a *child*). Open the stack, click the first to switch back, then mark the third — the tree keeps **both** branches, so your history is never lost:

- [ ] draft the launch plan <!-- @id:now-draft -->
- [ ] handle the review notes <!-- @id:now-review -->
- [ ] cut the release <!-- @id:now-release -->

In the stack, hover a node for its actions — `↑` **Bump** lifts that entry to the top as the current now, jumps to it, and flips it to `[/]` (like `Alt+W`), *without* branching (unlike marking, which nests a child) and leaving its children where they are; alongside set-as-current, prune, and remove.

## 12. Putting it together

A real slice of a plan — every status, priority, tag, and link at once. The priorities tint their rows, the cancelled line is struck through, the metadata stays dimmed. Hover any task, click a `children:` / `parent:` / `dependsOn:` / `movedTo:` lens to jump, or `Alt+T` a tag to find more like it. The task text itself is plain Markdown — inline `code`, **bold**, and *italic* all render in place.

